  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the constant multiple and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(z\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(xy)) \\\\  & =z\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(xy)) \\\\  & =z\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(xy)^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(xy) \\\\  & =z\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(xy)^{2}}}\\cdot (x) \\\\  & =\\frac{xz}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
